{%- comment -%}
  Post-entry page: three required questions, then the entry-ladder widget.

  Deliberately contains NO OFFER. The BOGO is released once, on draw day, as the
  consolation prize for not winning (spec 7.1). A full-price store link stays
  here so an entrant who wants to buy on day 3 is never blocked.

  Q1 (household) gates the duration claim on the day-30 offer: a shared bar does
  not last 25 days, so a family answer suppresses the months claim entirely.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign endpoint = 'https://entries.realskincare.com/api/giveaway'
  assign set_handle = 'sensitive-skin-starter-set'
  assign set_image = 'https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0270/1911/6579/files/frame-01-what-arrives.jpg?v=1785635169'
-%}

{{ 'giveaway.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<section class="gv-entered" data-gv-entered>
  {%- comment -%}
    This used to read "You're in." — true (submitting earns the base entry) and precisely
    the phrase that tells someone they are finished. Measured on day one of the paid
    campaign: 11 people submitted, 3 clicked the confirmation link. 27%.

    Confirming is worth +2 entries — triple the base entry — and it is what puts the
    profile on the list at all, so an unconfirmed entrant receives no nurture email and
    cannot be credited as anyone's referrer. So the headline now names the step that is
    still outstanding, and the base entry is reassurance underneath rather than the
    headline. Do not restore a headline that implies completion.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <h1>One more step — check your email.</h1>
  <p class="gv-lead">
    We just sent a confirmation link. <strong>Click it and you get 2 bonus entries</strong> —
    three times what entering just earned you. It can take a minute to arrive, and it
    sometimes lands in spam or Promotions.
  </p>
  <p class="gv-lead-sub">Your entry is already counted. Confirming is what multiplies it.</p>

  {%- comment -%}
    Shown ONLY to someone who named a referrer, and only while they are still
    unconfirmed — revealed by giveaway.js from the hasReferrer flag on
    GET /api/giveaway/entries.

    Why it exists: §5 pays the referrer +5 only once the friend they referred
    CONFIRMS. Measured 2026-08-22, six of seven referral pairs in the system were
    stuck at exactly this step. Everything else on this page argues from what the
    reader gets; this is the one line that argues from what someone else loses.

    It never names the friend. The endpoint returns a boolean precisely so that
    this page cannot disclose one entrant's referrer to anyone who knows their
    address.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <p class="gv-referral-stake" data-gv-referral-stake hidden>
    <strong>Your friend gets +5 entries too — but only after you click.</strong>
    Right now they have nothing from referring you.
  </p>

  <form class="gv-survey" data-step="required">
    <fieldset>
      <legend>Who's the soap for?</legend>
      <label><input type="radio" name="household" value="solo" required> Just me</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="household" value="couple"> Me and my partner</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="household" value="family"> My whole family</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="household" value="gift"> It's a gift</label>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset>
      <legend>What's your #1 skin frustration?</legend>
      <label><input type="radio" name="frustration" value="dry" required> Dry and flaky</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="frustration" value="reactive"> Itchy and reactive</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="frustration" value="fragrance"> Fragrance sets me off</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="frustration" value="ingredients"> Ingredient concerns</label>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset>
      <legend>What are you using now?</legend>
      <label><input type="radio" name="currentBrand" value="cerave" required> CeraVe</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="currentBrand" value="cetaphil"> Cetaphil</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="currentBrand" value="dove"> Dove</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="currentBrand" value="natural_competitor"> Dr. Squatch or Native</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="currentBrand" value="natural_brand"> Another natural brand</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="currentBrand" value="whatever"> Whatever's on sale</label>
    </fieldset>

    <button type="submit">Save — and get 3 bonus entries</button>
    <p class="gv-error" hidden role="alert"></p>
  </form>

  <div class="gv-ladder" data-gv-ladder hidden>
    <h2>Your entries: <span data-gv-count>1</span></h2>
    <ul>
      <li data-rung="confirm">Confirm your email — <strong>+2</strong></li>
      <li data-rung="survey">Answer 3 quick questions — <strong>+3</strong></li>
      <li data-rung="referral">Each friend who enters, names you, and confirms their own entry — <strong>+5</strong> (up to 10)</li>
      <li data-rung="instagram">Post and tag @realskincare_com — <strong>+3</strong></li>
      <li data-rung="upload">Upload a photo — <strong>+10</strong></li>
    </ul>

    <form class="gv-bonus" data-gv-bonus>
      <label for="gv-ig">Posted about us? Your Instagram handle <span>(+3)</span></label>
      <input id="gv-ig" name="igHandle" type="text" placeholder="@yourhandle" autocomplete="off">

      {%- comment -%}
        "photo", not "photo or video": validateUpload in
        agents/dashboard/routes/giveaway.js accepts jpg/jpeg/png/webp only, and
        uploadImageToShopifyCDN is image-only. Promising video would take the
        entrant's rights grant and then reject the file.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <label for="gv-file">Upload a photo <span>(+10)</span></label>
      <input id="gv-file" name="file" type="file" accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp">

      <label class="gv-rights">
        <input type="checkbox" name="rightsGranted" value="1">
        I'm happy for Real Skin Care to use my photo in its marketing.
      </label>

      <button type="submit">Claim my bonus entries</button>
      <p class="gv-bonus-error" hidden role="alert"></p>
      {%- comment -%}
        role="status" not role="alert": a success confirmation should be
        announced politely, without interrupting a screen reader mid-sentence.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="gv-bonus-ok" hidden role="status"></p>
    </form>

    <p class="gv-fine">Purchases do not earn entries.
      <a href="/pages/giveaway-official-rules">Official rules</a>.</p>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Shown only after the survey is saved — the moment of highest engagement, and
    holding it back keeps the +3 rung as the single ask on arrival.

    Full price, no code, no urgency. The BOGO is the day-30 consolation prize
    (spec 7.1), and a discount shown beside a sweepstakes entry invites the
    "buying improves my odds" reading the Official Rules explicitly deny. The
    line under the button is not decoration — it is that denial, restated where
    the buying decision actually happens.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <aside class="gv-next" data-gv-next hidden>
    <div class="gv-next-shot">
      <img src="{{ set_image }}&width=600" alt="The Sensitive Skin Moisturizing Set" width="600" height="600" loading="lazy">
    </div>
    <div class="gv-next-copy">
      <p class="gv-next-eyebrow">Don't want to wait for the draw?</p>
      <h2>The Sensitive Skin Moisturizing Set</h2>
      {%- comment -%}
        The Set is the Body Lotion + Body Cream — "eight ingredients across two
        products". It does NOT contain soap; the 36 bars are a separate prize
        component. An earlier draft here said the Set included the soap, which
        was simply false. Check the product description before editing this.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="gv-next-body">
        Three of these ship with the prize, one a year. Two products, eight
        ingredients, no fragrance — the body lotion and body cream that go
        alongside the soap you just entered for.
      </p>
      <p class="gv-next-price">$46.80</p>
      <a class="gv-next-cta" href="/products/{{ set_handle }}">See the Set</a>
      <p class="gv-next-fine">Buying doesn't change your entries.</p>
    </div>
  </aside>
</section>

<script>window.RSC_GIVEAWAY_ENDPOINT = {{ endpoint | json }};</script>
<script src="{{ 'giveaway.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Giveaway entered",
  "settings": [],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Giveaway entered" }]
}
{% endschema %}
